From: batya <batya@github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 21:16:18 +0600
Subject: [PATCH 15/16] feat(agent): the message log keeps what the agent did,
 not only what it asked
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Every call that makes, changes, removes or starts something now lands in the
window's message log, quietly - the tool and the name of what it acted on
("library_song_like: Провода и дождь"), with a robot's mark, and without a toast
in the middle of the screen. Reading the library, looking at statuses and moving
the window's mouse stay out: the log is what the agent did TO the studio.

The server decides by the tool's own wording (is_noteworthy) and takes the name of
the thing from what the tool was given or what the studio answered with
(acted_on) - an id never travels to the log and neither does anything a tool was
told in confidence. The window writes the line itself through the journal_note
bridge command, so both strings are on the five languages the studio speaks.
---
 app/App.tsx                    | 11 ++++++++
 app/i18n/yue2.ts               | 10 ++++++++
 crates/music-server/src/mcp.rs | 46 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 67 insertions(+)

diff --git a/app/App.tsx b/app/App.tsx
index e269ab9..c293c72 100644
--- a/app/App.tsx
+++ b/app/App.tsx
@@ -1524,6 +1524,17 @@ function AppContent() {
       },
     });
   }));
+  // The agent's own work lands in the message log quietly: no toast in the middle of
+  // the screen, just the record of what was done - the tool and what it acted on.
+  useBridgeCommand('journal_note', ({ tool, target }) => {
+    const ran = String(tool ?? '');
+    const acted = String(target ?? '');
+    if (!ran) return 'Nothing to note.';
+    noteJournal(acted
+      ? t('agentActionRanOn').replace('{tool}', ran).replace('{target}', acted)
+      : t('agentActionRan').replace('{tool}', ran), 'agent');
+    return 'Noted.';
+  });
   useBridgeCommand('library_song_like', ({ song_id, liked }) => {
     const song = songById(song_id);
     if (likedSongIds.has(song.id) !== (liked !== false)) toggleLike(song.id);
